---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Data Methodology"
  description="How World Freight Hub estimates freight rates, transit times, and confidence levels."
  canonical="/methodology/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="section">Data Methodology</h1>
    <h2>Confidence levels</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Verified (HIGH)</strong> — government, customs, port authority, or official carrier data.</li>
      <li><strong>Indicative (MEDIUM)</strong> — consistent across multiple credible industry sources.</li>
      <li><strong>Reported (LOW)</strong> — single company, forum, or personal source.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Freight rates & transit times</h2>
    <p>
      We do not publish live prices or schedules. Rate figures are indicative ranges with a
      stated last-updated date, source, and assumptions. Freight rates vary by carrier, season,
      cargo, container type, and surcharges.
    </p>
    <h2>Secondary verification</h2>
    <p>
      Core facts are cross-checked against at least two independent sources before publication.
      Single-source information is explicitly marked.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
